WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.970
- [Announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.490
this is the main event
you've all been waiting for,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.050
the release of iOS 14.5..

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:13.600
In one corner, Apple's CEO, Tim Cook.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.600
In the other, the Facebook
CEO, Mark Zuckerberg.

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:20.282
(bell ringing)

00:00:20.282 --> 00:00:24.120
(characters banging)
(characters punching)

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:24.953
(crowd cheering)

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:27.480
- Well, folks, that's gonna leave a mark.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.731
Pun intended.

00:00:28.731 --> 00:00:32.360
(crowd booing)
(cup clattering)

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.200
Uh.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.770
What we're seeing unfold in this fight

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.220
is quite complicated.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.550
In fact, you're probably thinking

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.500
what's this beef all about?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.680
Apple makes phones,
tablets, laptops and more.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.720
Facebook makes social networks.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.283
Why the slug fest?

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.340
The simple answer?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.290
Differing views of our privacy

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:55.000
and it's playing out big
time in Apple's new iOS 14.5.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.600
But that's just the first round.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.720
This is a fight that
could shape the future

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.560
of the internet

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.010
and certainly, the next wave of computing.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.710
Yeah, it's a lot.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.210
So I thought it was best to explain it

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.410
with the help of these guys.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.934
No, you cannot buy these

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.340
because they're just terrifying.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.670
(dramatic music)

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.270
Okay, let's explain this all,

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.650
starting with what brought this to a head.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.883
iOS 14.5.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.500
And a new feature called
App Tracking Transparency.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.380
Now, for years, every iPhone

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.200
has had a secret string
of numbers inside it.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.120
It's called the IDFA,
Identifier for Advertisers.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.750
We'll call it your very
own ad tracking number

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.769
and it's used to help apps identify you

00:01:37.769 --> 00:01:40.190
and know what you're up to on your phone.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:42.440
So for instance, say Mr. Cook,

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.453
let's call him user 098002,

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.440
has decided to relax and
download a new meditation app.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.460
The app records his number,
(app dinging)

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.740
and here's the thing,

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.300
the Facebook app and other apps

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.170
on his phone also have that number.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.050
If that same meditation app wants

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.180
to try to get Mr. Cook

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.530
on its mega super relaxing
subscription plan,

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.850
it can go to Facebook and say hey,

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:11.400
let me advertise to user 098002.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.100
If Facebook has that
number and there's a match,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.470
boom, the personalized ad shows up

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.520
in Mr. Cook's Facebook feed.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.310
There's another way this all used.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.400
Say that meditation app
shows ads in its feed.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.250
It can use Facebook's Ad Network,

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.690
which again uses that number

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.910
to keep track of your other interests

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.820
and feed you highly personalized ads.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.653
So you get it.

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:34.410
These user numbers are good for Facebook

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.680
and other social networks

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.010
that wanna know what
we're doing on our phones.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.280
And they're good for businesses

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.750
that want us to buy stuff.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.070
But now with iOS 14.5,

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.040
Apple turns off that
ad tracker by default.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.560
If an app wants to track
you using that number,

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.400
it will have to ask.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.400
If Mr. Cook taps Ask App Not to Track,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.280
then his meditation app
won't get his number.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.930
Apple is giving companies a chance

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.690
to plead their case with
this area right here

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.860
that explains what the
company uses the data for.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.740
Don't want those popups at all?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.690
You can opt out of all tracking

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.640
by going to Settings, Privacy, Tracking

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.890
and turning off Allow
Apps to Request to Track.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.730
All in all, this is Apple's big play

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.050
to give people a choice
whether they wanna be tracked.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.800
And chances are, more people are going

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.010
to tap Ask App Not to Track.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.650
And guess who isn't happy about that all?

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.782
Eminem, the rapper.

00:03:26.782 --> 00:03:27.770
(upbeat music)

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.400
Sorry, I mean Mark Zuckerberg.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.710
Our custom designs were rush ordered.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.130
See, Facebook's business is built

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.110
on personalized advertising.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.150
Instead of charging you to use Facebook,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.850
Facebook charges companies to advertise.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.860
These ads are targeted at you based

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.510
on everything Facebook knows about you.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.800
Here's an ad Facebook ran

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.350
in The Wall Street Journal
at the end of 2020.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.600
We're standing up to Apple for
small businesses everywhere.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.130
Many in the business community

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:56.630
have shared concerns about
Apple's forced software update,

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.190
which will limit businesses' ability

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.530
to run personalized ads

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.164
and reach their customers effectively.

00:04:02.164 --> 00:04:03.479
(bell dinging)
(crowd cheering)

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:04.410
(characters punching)

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.210
Facebook CFO, Dave Wehner,

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.150
was clear about how it will
impact Facebook directly

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.850
on a January 2021 earnings call.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:12.860
- [Dave] We continue to believe

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.090
that that will be a headwind
in the ads business.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:19.130
We're gonna have to be
providing a prompt asking people

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.130
for permission to use third-party data

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.650
to deliver personalized ads

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.820
and we do expect there
to be high opt-out rates

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.830
related to that.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.590
- [Joanna] The company
added that the Apple prompt

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.760
doesn't give enough
context about the benefits

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.440
of personalized ads.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.310
Still, while Facebook has said recently

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.840
that it won't have a big
impact to its own business,

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.450
Facebook seems to be acknowledging

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.540
that given the choice,

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.030
users would prefer not to be tracked.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.317
A Facebook spokesman said,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.230
"While Apple claims the
update is about privacy,

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.200
it's about forcing small businesses

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.020
and developers to charge for apps

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.420
that were once free,

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.920
hurting consumers in the process.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.550
Free, ad-supported services
have been essential

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.090
to the growth and
vitality of the internet,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.860
and we're joining others to
point out Apple's hypocrisy

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.130
and anti-competitive behavior."

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.277
An Apple spokesperson responded.

00:05:07.277 --> 00:05:09.330
"Apps and advertisers can continue

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:13.190
to track users across apps
and websites as before.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.040
App Tracking Transparency in iOS 14

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.650
simply requires that they
ask for users' permission

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.670
before sharing their data
with other companies.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.750
Supporting small businesses
has been at the heart

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.790
of the App Store since it was created

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.500
to help developers of all sizes develop,

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.360
test, and distribute
apps around the world."

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.040
The company also says it has
introduced new free tools

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.530
for advertisers to measure their campaigns

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.020
while respecting user privacy.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.930
As a company based on hardware sales

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.610
and more recently, more
subscription services,

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.360
Apple has long stood on
the side of user privacy.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.630
Here's Steve Jobs in 2010.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:53.630
- Privacy means people know
what they're signing up for

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.820
in plain English.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.620
And some people wanna share
more data than other people do.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.180
Ask 'em.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:01.927
Ask 'em every time.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.110
- [Joanna] And Cook has
taken over that mantle

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:07.090
and said this in January 2021.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:10.000
- If a business is built
on misleading users,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.150
on data exploitation,

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:15.370
on choices that are no choices at all,

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.090
then it does not deserve our praise.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.120
It deserves reform.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:25.120
At its foundation, ATT is about
returning control to users,

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.513
about giving them a say over
how their data is handled.

00:06:29.513 --> 00:06:31.659
(bell dinging)
(crowd cheering)

00:06:31.659 --> 00:06:32.492
(characters punching)

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:35.070
- But of course, there is
benefit to Apple's business.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.930
Mr. Cook and his team see privacy

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.360
and other security features,

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.420
like encryption as a selling point

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.380
of its hardware and software combo.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.100
So two men, two very
different business models

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.640
and two very different visions

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.850
of how technology and the
internet should work for us.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:53.150
And the future fights are
going to go way behind privacy.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:55.010
On that same earnings call from January,

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.420
Mark Zuckerberg said,

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.472
- [Mark] I do wanna highlight

00:06:57.472 --> 00:06:59.850
that we increasingly see Apple

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.360
as one of our biggest competitors.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.550
- [Joanna] He pointed out
products like iMessage competes

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.150
with Facebook's messaging business,

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.550
which includes WhatsApp,
Instagram and Facebook Messenger.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.890
- [Mark] Apple has every incentive

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.250
to use their dominant platform position

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.010
to interfere with how our apps

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.670
and other apps work,
which they regularly do

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:18.955
to preference their own.

00:07:18.955 --> 00:07:20.989
(bell dinging)
(crowd cheering)

00:07:20.989 --> 00:07:23.020
(characters punching)

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.670
- But where's this really heading?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.240
Literally our heads.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.980
The fight for the future of computers,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.250
augmented reality glasses.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.300
When the tech is ready

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.060
and these aren't just big, bulky headsets,

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:37.070
these glasses will probably
run an operating system made

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.850
by one of these companies.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.240
And it could be a fight
bigger than Android versus iOS

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.300
or Windows verse Mac.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.850
Facebook, which owns Oculus,

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.380
is investing heavily in the
software and hardware side

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.590
of glasses, and is planning
to release some smart glasses

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.020
in the next year.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.460
- I can't go into full product details yet

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.540
but they're gonna be the next step

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.740
on the road to augmented reality glasses.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.670
- [Joanna] Apple is
working on its own headset,

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.212
according to various reports

00:08:03.212 --> 00:08:05.000
and Tim Cook has shared his interest

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.090
in augmented reality for years now.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:11.550
- And I think AR can help
amplify the human connection.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:16.550
I've never been a fan of VR like that

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.630
because I think it does the opposite.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.115
- So you see, this change in iOS 14.5

00:08:21.115 --> 00:08:24.020
is just the start of this fight.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.861
You know what's not gonna
be happening any time soon?

00:08:26.861 --> 00:08:30.440
(groovy beach music)

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.961
As for who ultimately wins,

00:08:31.961 --> 00:08:33.320
there's not telling

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.470
but at least with iOS 14.5,

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.740
the winners are users

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.860
who have wanted control
of their privacy and data.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.450
Do you guys do anything else?

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.110
You just go to the gym all the time?

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.360
Tim Cook has the same
abs as Mark Zuckerberg.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.863
They're both ripped.

